Two notes on the judgement calls: rejected items are chased (not excluded) because the underlying evidence is still required — rejection describes the document received, not the requirement. And the held lines are deliberately kept out of both the packet *and* the chase list; "not yet decided" is a distinct state from "outstanding," and collapsing the two is the single most likely error in a chat-plus-tracker setup.
